WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:03.810
The First rule of Fight Club?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.750
I mean, of Geopolitics?

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.200
There are no power vacuums.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.630
The current president of Turkey, Recep Tayyip
Erdoğan, knows this rule very well.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:17.720
In recent years he has shown the Western world
that geopolitical weaknesses are opportunities

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.410
for expansion and conquest for whoever is
able to seize them.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.070
Erdogan's motto is "carpe diem".

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.980
Ambiguity, double-dealing and diplomatic skill
have made Turkey an important player in the

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.220
Mediterranean in recent years.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.879
Are we sure that this strategy doesn't have
gray areas and in the long run, someone doesn't

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:38.539
come along to present the bill?

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:43.739
After all, as Giulio Andreotti would have
said, power consumes those who don't have

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:47.309
it, so we should be careful of those who crave
it at all costs.

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:55.100
To understand the rise of the Turkish foreign
policy we have to go back twenty years: in

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.390
2002.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.896
Erdogan got off to a roaring start in the
immediate post-election period in 2002: the

00:00:59.896 --> 00:01:04.620
president had impressed everyone with his
foreign policy based on the strategy of "no

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.220
problems with the neighbourhood".

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:11.750
He had obtained a cease-fire with the Kurds
of the PKK; he had normalized relations with

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:17.230
the much disputed Armenia; he had eased tensions
in the Aegean with the Greeks.

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:22.970
And he had increased trade with the Arab states
of the Gulf, while continuing to negotiate

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.550
membership with the European Union.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:31.140
Yet, over the years, this strategy of détente
has been progressively replaced by a vision

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.830
that some have called neo-Ottoman.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:39.190
The goal: to bring back a large part of the
Mediterranean under the Turkish sphere of

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.190
influence.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.210
The coup attempt of July Twelve Sixsteen and
the early elections of Twelve Eighteen (carried

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:51.310
out in a climate that was anything but democratic)
quickly made clear how urgent it was to stabilize

00:01:51.310 --> 00:02:07.710
the country's home front.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:13.330
Not an easy task, made even more complex by
a Turkish lira subject to continuous devaluations,

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:18.860
by soaring prices as well as by a general
slowdown in the economy, which is increasingly

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.209
tied to hydrocarbon exports.

00:02:21.209 --> 00:02:26.610
Certainly, in recent years, Erdogan's Turkey
has made important steps especially in military

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:31.659
technology and in the defense industry (the
production of drones, is now the flagship

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:36.590
of the Turkish war industry), and we must
not forget the ambitious space program recently

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.989
launched by the government.

00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:43.890
However, investment demand remains high and
Erdoğan's undiplomatic attitude is certainly

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.439
not encouraging Western investors.

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:51.390
Simply think of the corruption scandals, the
censorship of the media and the shutdown of

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:56.719
Twitter, YouTube and Wikipedia in 2014, the
lack of respect for minorities, the amendment

00:02:56.719 --> 00:03:01.919
to the Constitution, up to the most recent
incident with Von der Leyen's chair, or the

00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:07.669
dismissal of Central Bank Governor Naci Agbal,
appointed last November 2020 in the midst

00:03:07.669 --> 00:03:12.969
of a major currency crisis and removed just
four months later following an interest rate

00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:13.969
hike.

00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:19.040
In an attempt to distract his citizens from
the country's shaky domestic situation, President

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.700
Erdoğan has shifted their attention to foreign
dynamics, riding on nationalistic sentiments,

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.659
focusing on the project of regaining, at an
international level, the ancient Turkish role

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:27.900
in the Muslim world.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.680
For this reason, Ankara's aim has come to
be based on a maritime strategy in the Mediterranean:

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:45.120
the "Blue Homeland" strategy.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:52.560
First theorized in 2006 by Turkish naval admirals
Cem Gürdeniz and Cihat Yaycı, the Blue Homeland

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.760
(Turkish: Mavi Vatan) is a geopolitical and
economic doctrine that aims to provide a legal

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.159
basis for Turkey's expansionist ambitions
in the Mediterranean.

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:04.779
Revived by President Erdoğan in recent years,
and increasingly popular among Turkey's military

00:04:04.779 --> 00:04:09.469
and political elites, the Mavi Vatan theory
aims to redraw Exclusive Economic Zones (EEZs)

00:04:09.469 --> 00:04:13.250
in the waters of the Aegean and Black Seas
in Turkey's favor.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:19.750
The doctrine - outside of alleged pseudo-Ottoman
irredentist motivations - has a clear economic

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:20.750
purpose.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.950
But for a better understanding we have to
slingshot back to 2015, when large amounts

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:29.570
of natural gas were found on the seabed in
the Eastern Mediterranean.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:35.410
Projections at the time estimated deposits
of 3.5 trillion cubic meters of gas, mainly

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:39.950
located in the EEZ of Cyprus, Israel and Egypt.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:45.160
Quantity that would make even King Midas turn
pale - we are still talking about Anatolia

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.160
after all.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:51.330
For Turkey, enlarging its EEZ would potentially
mean getting its hands on that wealth.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:57.440
A scenario that fascinates also the European
Union, eager to free itself from its dependence

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.570
on Russian gas.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:05.100
Now, the origin of the dispute in the Aegean
dates back to the Cypriot conflict of 1974,

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.790
and the consequent division of the island
into two areas of interest: the Turkish Republic

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:15.000
of Northern Cyprus (not recognized by the
international community but only by Turkey,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.470
which occupies its waters illegally and the
Republic of Cyprus, member of the EU since

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:24.910
2004, supported by the government of Athens
and the UN.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:30.060
In the last decade, the discovery of deposits
off the coast of Cyprus has allowed the governments

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:35.500
involved to ride the ethnic conflict on the
island, transforming it into a metaphorical

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:41.150
gold rush that has quickly involved even states
of the European Union, including Italy.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:45.650
In theory, the division of the territorial
waters of the Anatolian peninsula and the

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:50.210
Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus should
follow the United Nations Convention on the

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:55.650
Law of the Sea (UNCLOS), according to which
each state has the right to apply its jurisdiction

00:05:55.650 --> 00:06:00.080
up to 12 miles (about 22 km) from its coast.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:05.190
Yet the use of this method generates controversies,
especially because of the presence of some

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:11.030
Greek islands that, being close to the Turkish
coast, create irregularities in the tracing

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.030
of boundaries.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.440
This is the case of the island of Kastellorizo.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:19.360
In Italy we have a famous movie about Kastelorizon:
Mediterraneo, Mediterranean Sea.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.430
Here’s a quote from it: "We were being sent
on a mission to Megisti, a remote island in

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.530
the Aegean, the smallest, the farthest away
island.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.260
No strategic importance.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:30.260
Zero."

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:36.850
Megisti, also known as Kastellorizo, was an
Italian possession from the 20s until 1947,

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.970
when it was given back to Greece.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:46.370
Distant 2 km from the Turkish coasts and 570
km from the Greek ones, the island of Megisti/Kastelorizo

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:52.180
represents one of the main nodes of the territorial
issue between Greece and Turkey in the Dodecanese:

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:58.000
on one side Kastellorizo allows Athens to
claim the legitimacy of the surrounding waters,

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.900
according to the United Nations Convention
on the Law of the Sea, but on the other side

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.090
it reduces the Turkish Exclusive Economic
Zone (EEZ).

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.310
Today Kastellorizo is of extreme strategic
importance.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:12.870
The Water Convention has never been signed
by Turkey, as it was considered inconvenient

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.970
for its own national interests.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:21.550
For the EEZ, the Turkish president is absolutely
not willing to give in: already in 2019, Erdoğan

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:26.880
signed two bilateral agreements with al-Sarraj,
the Libyan president of the Government of

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:32.780
National Accord (GNA), one on military cooperation
and one concerning the borders of the respective

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.350
maritime EEZs.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:40.270
In the first one, Erdoğan offered military
equipment - thus violating the UN arms embargo

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:45.460
on Libya - in exchange for a second agreement,
which would concern the jurisdiction over

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.870
the sea borders between the two states.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:53.310
This document would authorize the exploration
of the seabed, following the (Turkish!) theory

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.900
of the continental plates and ignoring the
law of the sea.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:02.370
In this way Turkey would actually expand its
sovereignty to the areas of the East Mediterranean

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:07.490
Sea where there are important gas fields (to
name a few, the Leviathan gas field, of four

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:13.580
hundred and fifty billion square meters, the
Zohr of eight hundred and billion m3, and

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:18.000
the Noor Gas Field, this one estimated to
be three times larger than Zohr).

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.730
In 45 years of dispute, every time the European
Court rejected the Turkish hope for a recognition

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:27.230
of the extension of its maritime borders,
Ankara responded with the signing of partial

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:30.350
agreements (such as those with Bulgaria, Romania
and Russia), drawing new Exclusive Economic

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.350
Zones.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:35.820
This agreement, however, challenges the rules
of international law and conceals the project

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:41.740
of an alleged corridor of security and assistance
between Turkey and Libya, a real "highway"

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:47.290
under Turkish control to replicate what has
already been tested in the EEZ in the Cyprus

00:08:47.290 --> 00:09:01.670
waters. he European Council has therefore
rejected the agreement, confirming its support

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:06.800
to Greece and Cyprus, but Turkey - which is
still part of the NATO alliance - has nevertheless

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:11.550
started its research activities in the Cypriot
EEZ.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:16.130
Good neighborly relationships, kind of like
when the pain-in-the-ass neighbor above you

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:20.750
makes noise all night and then accuses you
of being the stalker when you point out that

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.400
maybe he's gone too far.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:27.110
However, interests related to the extraction
of natural resources are not the only ones

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:32.560
at stake: the agreement with Libya, in fact,
hinders the realization of the EastMed Gas

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:37.400
Pipeline, a project conceived in 2013 for
a 1900 km pipeline, mainly underwater, that

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:43.130
would connect gas deposits in Israel and Cyprus
to European markets passing through Greece

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:47.990
(Crete and mainland), up to, possibly, the
coasts of Apulia.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:53.860
The pipeline would then cross the EEZ claimed
by Turkey, allowing it to secure a role in

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:54.860
this business.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:58.950
Possible nervousness from Europe does not
frighten Ankara, which continues in its plan

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:04.920
to gain a strong position in the Mediterranean,
aware that no NATO ship will ever fire against

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:07.450
Turkish ships, still formally allied.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:12.490
As of today, there have been no relevant diplomatic
protests to contain the Turkish expansionism.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:18.140
But in the meantime, the increasing relationship
between Erdoğan and al-Sarraj is rapidly

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.710
turning Libya into a Turkish outpost in the
Western Mediterranean, an outpost destined

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:27.380
first of all to block the possibility of a
collaboration between Cyprus, Egypt, Greece

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:32.089
and Israel for the creation of a gas transport
line able to cut off the Turks.

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:37.170
Libya is no stranger to Erdogan's flattery:
some projects between Turkey and Libya involved

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:42.490
the construction of three power plants, a
commercial center and an airfield in Tripoli,

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:46.510
for an increase in import-export of about
5 billion dollars.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:51.580
All this was possible on the one hand with
the exit of the United States from Libya in

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:57.440
2019 and on the other hand with the Italian
and French hesitation to take a position in

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:13.150
a country devastated by NATO bombings 
in 2011.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:18.320
Also on the issue of migration flows, Turkey
has gradually replaced Italy in the management

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.250
of relations with Libya.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:26.029
already in the summer of 2020 Turkey has managed
to acquire control of the Libyan Coast Guard

00:11:26.029 --> 00:11:30.611
patrol boats (donated by Italy), thus souring
relations with Rome.

00:11:30.611 --> 00:11:34.060
The event, in fact, goes far beyond a "handover".

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:39.650
The patrol boats, which now have Turkish instructors
on board, were financed with the aim of increasing

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:45.010
the efficiency of patrols in one of the most
sensitive traffic areas for migratory flows

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.470
from Africa to Europe, Italy first and foremost.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:54.010
In essence, Turkey has now secured management
of the two major migratory corridors between

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:59.140
Africa and Italy: the land route from the
Anatolian peninsula to the Balkans and the

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:01.760
sea route across the Mediterranean.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:06.680
If we add to this the fact that the Libyan
SAR zone (that is the search and rescue area)

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:12.980
was desired, designed and paid for by Italy,
the impatience of the italian government with

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:18.310
Erdoğan's aggressive foreign policy appears
at least understandable, if not acceptable.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:23.420
And that's not all, Turkey has managed to
penetrate another nation: Albania. from the

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:28.240
construction sector to the banking sector,
Turkey is gradually entering the Balkans,

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.710
first of all by taking advantage of the historical
bonds with this region.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:35.560
You know, the Balkans were under the Ottomans
for four centuries.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.779
And they still have a significant presence
of Muslim believers.

00:12:38.779 --> 00:12:44.210
The Turks have come back to Tirana, once again
filling a diplomatic space neglected by Rome

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.520
and other EU countries.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:50.510
Since 2020, Turkey has started to take care
of the training of the national armed forces.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:56.300
In addition, the Albanian parliament has allocated
funds necessary for the purchase of the famous

00:12:56.300 --> 00:13:01.300
Bayraktar Tb2 drones designed by the son-in-law
of the Turkish president.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:06.470
And among other things, the bulky Turkish
presence has also generated fears among the

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:11.640
non-Muslim Albanian community, worried about
a possible hardening of lifestyles in the

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:12.640
country.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.153
Erdoğan's aspirations do not stop at the
exclusively territorial reconquest of Turkish

00:13:15.153 --> 00:13:17.100
supremacy in the Mediterranean.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:20.800
As already mentioned, the president dreams
of a Turkey rich in energy resources, strong,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:25.520
able to become a point of reference also in
religious terms to recompose the Arab world.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:30.470
And this is where the decision to turn the
Hagia Sofia museum and the church of St. Savior

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:35.770
in Chora into mosques comes in, a project
that is not well liked by a nation not quite

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:37.890
friendly to Turkey: Egypt.

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:44.000
An open supporter of Haftar, Egypt has the
United Arab Emirates and Sunni Saudi Arabia

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.020
on its side.

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:49.990
Egypt, because of its proximity to Libya,
has been one of the few to make tangible moves

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:56.670
to counter Turkish aspirations in Cyrenaica,
where, the subsoil is rich in hydrocarbons,

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:01.610
and has repeatedly threatened the Turks of
heavy military intervention if armed clashes

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.380
spread east of Sirte.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:08.750
In addition, Al Sisi has immediately stipulated
agreements with the Greeks regarding the extension

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.029
of their own Exclusive Economic Zones.

00:14:11.029 --> 00:14:14.440
This obviously ignored Turkey’s plans for
its own EEZ.

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:21.250
But it’s not all: since 2003, Turkish trade
in the Horn of Africa has grown considerably,

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:26.960
from 5 to the current 25 billion dollars,
expanding Ankara's diplomatic network from

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.640
12 to 49 African embassies.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:35.920
The first to establish trusting relations
was Sudan in 2018, with the signing of a $100

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:41.000
million agreement to let the Turks conduct
oil exploration in the Abyei district.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:46.930
Sudan also assigned Turkey thousands of square
kilometers of farmland for investment purposes.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:51.940
And then there's Somalia, which, according
to Erdogan, has directly invited the Turks

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:55.459
to conduct explorations off its desert coast.

00:14:55.459 --> 00:14:59.980
Let's not always forget the war industry:
In the Horn of Africa, especially in Ethiopia,

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:03.970
Turkey has captured the hearts of the Ethiopian
Prime Minister - let's remember, awarded the

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:10.950
Nobel Peace Prize - and sold him him armored
vehicles, TAI Anka UAVs and Bayraktar Tb2

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:11.950
drones.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:17.470
The army of Aby Ahmed's government was saved
from defeat in the war thanks to the Turkish

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:22.680
drones, when the Tigrinya rebels were no more
than 200 km from the capital.

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:28.010
At the beginning, Erdogan's adventure in the
Horn of Africa was promoted as a humanitarian

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.010
intervention.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:33.589
A humanitarian intervention which, however,
included the construction of a military base

00:15:33.589 --> 00:15:43.000
worth 50 million dollars in Mogadishu.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:49.140
This was meant to be a gateway to East Africa.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:54.730
The intervention included also the concession
of Suakin Island by Sudan for the next 99

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:58.530
years in order to build a civilian and military
port.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:04.700
And also in 2020, Turkish forces have been
involved in training a third of the Somali

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:08.700
armed forces.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:17.269
The commitment is to equip the Somali national
army in the fight against the radical Islamic

00:16:17.269 --> 00:16:18.480
al-Shabaab militia.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.480
An attitude that denotes a certain medium
to long term vision.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:26.959
Turkish interest has then expanded to Niger
and Chad, where Turkey has once again taken

00:16:26.959 --> 00:16:32.790
advantage - just like Russia - of the withdrawal
of the former French colonial power, acting

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:35.450
as an allied and neighboring force.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:40.480
Erdogan has leveraged on the fact of having
a common religion (Islam) with this region

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:44.790
and exploited the anti-French feelings of
the population.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:49.330
Turkey has therefore expanded its area of
influence to the Sahel region, a success that

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:53.839
needs to be added to what has already been
achieved in the former Italian colonies of

00:16:53.839 --> 00:16:54.839
Libya and Somalia.

00:16:54.839 --> 00:17:00.339
All of this denotes a foreign policy capable
of exploiting conflicts, tensions and power

00:17:00.339 --> 00:17:06.449
vacuums, which is increasingly expanding from
the Mediterranean into the African hinterland.

00:17:06.449 --> 00:17:09.620
The real questions at this point are many:
how will President Erdoğan react if, faced

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:12.120
with yet another episode of Ottoman machismo,
NATO forces or EU member states decide to

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.120
retaliate?

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:16.000
Will he create the next power vacuum to be
filled?

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:20.700
Will the conflict between Ukraine and Russia
mark a rapprochement between Erdoğan and

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:21.700
Putin?

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:26.050
